url: "https://eivimeycook.github.io/Data-Code_Society/"
abstract: >-
  A question-by-question FAQ for the assessment form used at the SORTEE 2026
  conference hackathon, led by the SORTEE Advocacy Committee, on data and code
  availability and quality in journals published by ecology and evolution
  societies. Covers how to judge whether a paper's data and code are archived,
  accessible, licensed and documented, and how contributions are credited using
  Dragon Kill Points.
keywords:
  - open data
  - open code
  - data sharing
  - code sharing
  - reproducibility
  - research transparency
  - hackathon
  - scholarly publishing
  - journal policy
  - SORTEE
